!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
! $$Param chan...
!    These are intensity and parameter levels or moves.
!    They can be hard levels or references to presets and palettes.
!    These can appear in cues, submasters, presets and palettes.
!    Presets can have hard levels or palette references.
!    Palettes can only have hard levels.
!    The parameter numbers are gotten from $$ParamType.
!       param@level     parameter at a specific level(0-255,0-32767)
!       param@IPn        parameter at intensity palette n
!       param@FPn        parameter at focus palette n
!       param@CPn        parameter at color palette n
!       param@BPn        parameter at beam palette n
!       param@PRn        parameter at preset n
!       param@Gn#level   parameter at gel n
!       param@.Gn#level  parameter at gel with spectrum match n
!       param@:Gn#level  parameter at gel with hybrid match n
!       param@Qn         parameter at cue n
!    If a parameter is asserted, blocked, or both, then an
!    a, b, c or k will appear before the reference or level.
!       1@b127   intensity is blocked at 127
!       1@c127   intensity is auto blocked at 127
!       2@kPR2   pan is blocked & asserted at preset 2
!       1@a0     intensity is asserted (Not a Move!)
!    If a parameter is nulled or released, then a
!    n or r will appear before the reference or level.
!       1@n0     intensity is nulled (Not a Move!
!       1@r0     intensity is released (Not a Move!)
!    Note that asserted/nulled/released parameters do not
!    have moves so the level should be ignored.
! 
! $$ParamTimes          Chan, Param, Time ('M' =manual, '-' =none), Delay
! $$ColorFade           Chan, Param, Fadetype, optional times in percent
! $$MarkCue             Chan, Param, Mark Cue
! $$EffectChan          Effect, Chan, Parameters
! $$EffectData          Effect, Attribute, Value
 
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
! Cues
! $CueList n      All subsequent cues are in cuelist n
!                 Cue lists can have a TEXT secondary and the following flags:
! $$IntensityMaster
! $$Independent
! $$HTP           HTP
! $$Assert        Assert
! $$SoloMode      Solo Mode
! $$Data          Ext Links
! $$Master        Slider mode, see comment, default=Master
! $$BackFrom1st   see comment
! $$GoFromLast    see comment
! $$Stomp         see comment
! $$Exclude       see comment
! $$Control       number, fader mode, min, max, buttons 1-3 id/arg
! 
! $Cue:           All cues not in the first cue list and those
!                 with more than one digit after the decimal point
! $$Text          Cue/Part label
! $$Assert        Assert
! $$Block         Block
! $$IntBlock      IntBlock
! 
! The following cue times use this format:  Fade time, Delay time,
!                 Use default fadetime (1=true, 0=false, M=manual),
!                 Use default delay time (1=true, 0=false)
! $$TimeUp        Up times
! $$TimeDown      Down times
! $$TimePosition  Focus times
! $$TimeColor     Color times
! $$TimeGraphic   Beam times
! 
! $$Rate          Rate (100 = normal)
! $$Follow        Auto-follow time counting from previous cue start
! $$Hang          Auto-follow time counting from previous cue completion
! $$Action        Stop/Execute, Target
! $$Action        UDP/MIDI, String
! $$Curve         Curve (0.01 .. 9999.99)
! $$Link list/cue Link to or from a cue not in the first list or to
!                 one with more than one digit after the decimal point
! $$AlertTime     Cue Alert Time
! $$CueNotes      Cue Notes
! $$SceneText     Scene Text
! $$SceneEnd      Scene End flag
! 
! $$ChanMove      Intensity moves
! Chan            Tracked levels
 
$CueList 1
   Text SETUP
 
